e_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7t03Ya","user":{"login":"jebbyk","id":40975486,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwOTc1NDg2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40975486?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jebbyk","html_url":"https://github.com/jebbyk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jebbyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jebbyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jebbyk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jebbyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jebbyk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jebbyk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jebbyk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jebbyk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jebbyk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-03T10:23:08Z","updated_at":"2026-03-03T10:23:08Z","body":"is there any chance this PR gonna add an abbylity to retrieve an unlit albedo buffer too in compositor effect scripts? ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3990058522/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3990967442","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100710#issuecomment-3990967442","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100710","id":3990967442,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7t4VSS","user":{"login":"BadMachine","id":50546204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNTQ2MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50546204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BadMachine","html_url":"https://github.com/BadMachine","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BadMachine/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BadMachine/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BadMachine/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BadMachine/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BadMachine/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BadMachine/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BadMachine/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BadMachine/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BadMachine/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-03T13:10:09Z","updated_at":"2026-03-03T13:10:23Z","body":"> is there any chance this PR gonna add an abbylity to retrieve an unlit albedo buffer too in compositor effect scripts?\r\n\r\n@jebbyk \r\nHi! This PR is focused specifically on exposing LightStorage to RenderData for accessing light source buffers. Retrieving an unlit albedo buffer is outside its scope.\r\n\r\nHowever, there's a related [proposal](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/10396) that covers exactly this - accessing more common buffers (it also mentions unshaded color) through RenderSceneBuffersRD for use in CompositorEffect scripts","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3990967442/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3992906865","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100710#issuecomment-3992906865","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100710","id":3992906865,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7t_uxx","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-03T18:41:32Z","updated_at":"2026-03-03T18:41:32Z","body":"> Will need another discussion in the rendering meeting whether we see any roadblocks to exposing this in this manner but I think it's fairly safe.\r\n\r\n@BastiaanOlij Is there someone else you feel would be able to give a second opinion on the safety and long term impact of this new public API? I figure maybe this is suitable for David and/or Skyth to weigh in on...?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3992906865/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4008912155","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100710#issuecomment-4008912155","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100710","id":4008912155,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7u8yUb","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-06T01:31:53Z","updated_at":"2026-03-07T12:45:25Z","body":"> is there any chance this PR gonna add an abbylity to retrieve an unlit albedo buffer too in compositor effect scripts?\r\n\r\nKeep in mind here that Godot isn't a deferred renderer and thus doesn't have an unlit albedo buffer.\r\nAll of the render buffers are currently exposed through `RenderSceneBuffersRD` but you just need to know their names. We're hesitant to document those too directly because once done, they are set in stone, while these are things we want to be able to change without worrying about breaking peoples implementations. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4008912155/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4008926208","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100710#issuecomment-4008926208","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100710","id":4008926208,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7u81wA","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-06T01:35:17Z","updated_at":"2026-03-06T01:35:17Z","body":"> > Will need another discussion in the rendering meeting whether we see any roadblocks to exposing this in this manner but I think it's fairly safe.\r\n> \r\n> @BastiaanOlij Is there someone else you feel would be able to give a second opinion on the safety and long term impact of this new public API? I figure maybe this is suitable for David and/or Skyth to weigh in on...?\r\n\r\nIt's fairly unlikely access to these buffers will need to change. What is very likely to change and break from version to version is the contents of these buffers. We may add or change fields related to the light data. It's one of the reasons to mark these as experimental and point to Godots source for anyone that actually wants to do something with this.\r\n\r\nThe realisation with features like this, and compositor effects in general, is that we're working very close to how the rendering engine works and we're walking a really fine line between enabling features power users really want, and limiting our ability to improve the rendering engine.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4008926208/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4465762718","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100710#issuecomment-4465762718","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100710","id":4465762718,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCi4hng","user":{"login":"peanut250","id":209579534,"node_id":"U_kgDODH3uDg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/209579534?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/peanut250","html_url":"https://github.com/peanut250","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peanut250/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peanut250/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peanut250/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peanut250/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peanut250/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peanut250/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peanut250/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peanut250/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peanut250/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-16T05:14:11Z","updated_at":"2026-05-16T05:14:11Z","body":"@BadMachine Hey, I'm trying to sample the shadow map, does this PR expose the directional light projection matrix somewhere? I see the four matrices in the directional light buffer which look like some kind of projection pe